  "infoBreatheBody": "Slow belly breathing and gentle relaxation. Letting the muscles go is part of the training. Today's parts:",
  "infoHabitsBody": "Small habits for during the day, not timed sessions. Tick each one when you have done it today; tap again to untick. Habits never affect your streak or level.",
  "infoRestTitle": "Your plan week",
  "infoRestBody": "Your plan runs in 7-day weeks starting on the day you joined. Days 1 to 6 are training days and day 7 is a rest day, when only breathing is planned. Muscles recover on rest days, and a rest day never breaks your streak.",
  "infoStreakBody": "Days in a row with at least one completed session. Your weekly rest day never breaks it, and missed days start a new streak with no penalty.",
  "infoWeekRingBody": "Sessions completed since Monday. The ring on the streak card shows training days this week out of 6; the 7th day is for rest.",
  "infoHoldBody": "The longest hold the app has guided you through. A phone cannot measure your muscles, so this is the programmed hold you completed, not a measurement.",
  "infoLevelsTitle": "How levels work",
  "infoLevelsBody": "Each level adds longer holds or more reps. A plan week is 6 training days and 1 rest day inside the week. The next level unlocks when you finish this level's training days and have trained on at least 5 of the last 7 days. You can repeat or step down a level any time.",
  "infoCheckInTitle": "About check-ins",
  "infoCheckInBody": "One question about your goal, answered now and again every 4 weeks, so you can compare your own answers side by side. There are no predictions or scores from other people.",

  "infoGoalTitle": "What this plan includes",
  "infoGoalBladder": "Slow holds and quick squeezes, plus squeezing before coughs, lifts and standing up. Daily habits for after-dribble and sudden urges.",
  "infoGoalErection": "Standard levels with stronger holds from Level 3, bridges and squats, and a weekly brisk walking goal.",
  "infoGoalEjaculation": "Standard levels with more relaxation: reverse Kegels and extra breathing every day, so you learn to let go as well as squeeze.",
  "infoGoalSurgery": "Gentler holds of up to 10 seconds with 4 seconds of rest. Starts only after the catheter is removed and your care team agrees.",
